# Currents

Next.js full-stack app (App Router) with PostgreSQL. Single package at the repo root — no separate API service in V1.

## Repo map

```text
app/                         pages + route handlers (thin)
components/                  shared UI composition
components/ui/               shadcn primitives only
lib/                         shared helpers (incl. lib/db.ts → pool)
db/                          pg pool + SQL migration runner
infra/docker/                Compose (Postgres; optional web profile)
infra/database/migrations/   versioned *.sql (source of truth for schema)
```

## Call chain

```text
page (server) → lib/ helper → getPool() / query
route handler → lib/ helper (thin)
```

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only at the smallest interactive subtree.
- Business SQL and pool access live in `lib/` or `db/` — not inline in large pages.
- Schema changes are new `infra/database/migrations/NNNN_description.sql` files; never edit an applied migration.
- Local DB: `pnpm docker:up` (Postgres + migrate). Day-to-day Next: `pnpm dev` on the host.
